.TH LINUX-CONTAINER-EVIDENCE-AUDIT 1 "2026-10-28" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linux-container-evidence-audit \- validate and summarize offline container acceptance evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linux-container-evidence-audit
.RB [ --input " REPORT.jsonl" ]...
.RB [ --format " tsv|jsonl" ]
.RB [ --require-complete ]
.RB [ --help ]
.RB [ --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Summarize JSON Lines from the opt-in
.B linux-container-acceptance
runner for five Linux distribution targets. No Docker/Podman connection,
network access, package installation or configuration modification occurs.
All five container stages must pass before a target is reported PASS.
Unreported targets remain explicitly SKIP/NO_REPORT.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --input " REPORT.jsonl"
Read one local JSONL report (at most five options). Files must be regular,
not symlinks, at most 32 KiB, and contain exactly five canonical evidence rows.
.TP
.BI --format " tsv|jsonl"
Write tab-delimited output (default) or schema-versioned JSON Lines.
.TP
.B --require-complete
Return status 4 when any target is missing or has skipped stages.
.TP
.B --help
Display command-line usage.
.TP
.B --version
Display command version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Valid reports, without FAIL; unless strict completion is requested,
SKIP is permitted and remains visible.
.TP
.B 1
At least one target failed a reported stage.
.TP
.B 4
Strict completion required but one or more targets are incomplete.
.TP
.B Other nonzero
Invalid arguments or malformed/contradictory evidence.
.SH SECURITY AND LIMITATIONS
The reports are not cryptographic attestations. This command cannot prove
a source Git commit, image digest, host identity or container-engine version.
Successful container reports do not establish native kernel, firewall,
SELinux/AppArmor, systemd or VM compatibility.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR linux-container-acceptance (1),
.BR linux-distro-matrix (1)
